{"title":"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Pascal #18</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Cayley #8</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/9727b63f39628df696b9ecedae3bf312b9133ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD &lt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />. What is the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb31a177be729d00e07be87ccd9d2aa73923f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 23 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 26 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 27 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 28 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To make this easier to understand, we can drop down a height from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and name the resulting point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, which will be perpendicular. This forms rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc2637619787d327e60de3896432f2a24becdfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADEB$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a9191aefcf2eb237d1999486083ed78f6d515f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/5395b4380b8f21bc49b6affb62ab1af2c7a2ed14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = AD = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f29c3a94fb4aa712209c6bb7d66d2761be5f1256.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = AB = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" /> from rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc2637619787d327e60de3896432f2a24becdfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADEB$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, we can notice that we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">pythagorean theorem</a> with triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a9191aefcf2eb237d1999486083ed78f6d515f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, giving:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb30b9442318a413ee6a69a1713d8bbaed9ec9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 + DE^2 = CD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539ab61798baf455d97ecb222f6a784d60a180d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 + 4^2 = 5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/23178bda9c46b87c9cb460645e588da5aad6ab30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 + 16 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b91eb9fbe5b24c8fdcacd73b6d23936d8cd96ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 = 25 - 16 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be negative because it represents a side length. Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38303eb2650048880f0b99502f59b2e415fae78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\sqrt{9} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can then find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/5009b4697454b42ffe1d93f6cc0905168aac7c0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = AD + CE = 7 + 3 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"242\" height=\"16\" />, and we no longer need point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> or triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a9191aefcf2eb237d1999486083ed78f6d515f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Adding all of the side lengths together to find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a5f826f8dff02c8ca0a596f15a6d7f2dd31e800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + AB + BC + CD = 7 + 4 + 10 + 5 = 11 + 10 + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"435\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486b17fa100f0b700187411b98a20178a6159e61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=21 + 5 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"159\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can follow the same steps as solution 1.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>However, when using the pythagorean theorem to find CE, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539ab61798baf455d97ecb222f6a784d60a180d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 + 4^2 = 5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa581f6ebf396d9107036ef1ed8b11a0b8b724d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 = 5^2 - 4^2 = (5 - 4)(5 + 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6ab4d096906279e192eb6342df25ff22dec005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=1 \\times 9 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38303eb2650048880f0b99502f59b2e415fae78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\sqrt{9} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This ultimately leads to the same answer, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac94af50b9f005706a9501c429b643cf4423e8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.2\">Solution 1.2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can follow the same steps as solution 1. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>However, instead of using the pythagorean theorem, we can remember that 3-4-5 is a pythagorean triple. This gives us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d981341ed2e61e9de64b5b848e412aef2040793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This eventually leads to the same answer, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac94af50b9f005706a9501c429b643cf4423e8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal\">1999 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 14\">14</a>